node_modules/
dist/
.venv-live/
*.pyc
__pycache__/

# Working files for the AI assistants used to build this. They stay on the machine
# and out of the repository: they are written *to* an assistant rather than to a
# reader, and they carry personal framing that reads badly stripped of its context.
# The engineering reasoning they hold is in BUILD_PLAN.md, DATA_MODEL.md and the
# security audit, all of which are addressed to a person. Source comments and the
# audit still cite them by name — see the note in README.md.
AGENTS.md
CLAUDE.md

# A real Cronometer export must never enter this tree at all — not committed, not
# ignored, not present. These two rules are a backstop against an accidental
# `git add`, not permission to keep data here.
*.pdf
*.csv

# The synthetic fixtures are the one place CSVs belong. The negation has to name
# the files, not the directory: a `!test/fixtures/` line would only re-include the
# directory entry, and every .csv inside it would still match the rule above.
!test/fixtures/**/*.csv
